1
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:51,000
The memories. The madness. The music... The movie.

2
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Pink Floyd: The Wall is a music, drama film directed by Alan Parker.

3
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:21,000
A troubled rock star descends into madness in the midst of his
physical and social isolation from everyone.

4
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Pink, played by Bob Geldof.

5
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:51,000
Pink's Mother, played by Christine Hargreaves.

6
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:36,000
Pink's Father, played by James Laurenson.

7
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:21,000
Pink's Wife, played by Eleanor David.

8
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Young Pink, played by Kevin McKeon.

9
00:42:45,000 --> 00:42:51,000
Rock and Roll Manager, played by Bob Hoskins.

10
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:36,000
Pink Floyd – The Wall is a 1982 British live-action/animated musical surrealist drama film
directed by Alan Parker, based on Pink Floyd's 1979 studio album The Wall.

11
00:52:15,000 --> 00:52:21,000
The screenplay was written by Pink Floyd vocalist and bassist Roger
Waters, with animation sequences directed by Gerald Scarfe.

12
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
The Boomtown Rats' lead vocalist Bob Geldof made his film debut as rock star Pink, who, driven to neurosis by the pressures
of stardom and traumatic events in his life, constructs an emotional and mental wall to protect himself.

13
01:01:45,000 --> 01:01:51,000
However, this coping mechanism eventually
backfires, and Pink demands to be set free.

14
01:06:30,000 --> 01:06:36,000
Like its associated album, the film is highly metaphorical, and
frequently uses both visual and auditory symbolism throughout.

15
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:21,000
It features little dialogue, instead being driven by
the music from the album throughout.

16
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
The songs used in the film have several differences from their album versions, and two of the songs
included, "When the Tigers Broke Free" and "What Shall We Do Now?", do not appear on the album.

17
01:20:45,000 --> 01:20:51,000
Despite its turbulent production, the film received generally positive reviews, with praise for its
music and animation, and it has an established cult following among Pink Floyd fans.

18
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
The film explores themes of rock star, berlin wall,
paranoia, wall, descent into madness.

19
01:30:15,000 --> 01:30:21,000
The tone is emotional.
